<title>AUSTRALIA: MAXILINK YEAR NET PROFIT A$19.12 MLN.</title>
<headline>MAXILINK YEAR NET PROFIT A$19.12 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    11.60 vs 6.27</p>
<p>    Net				     19.12 vs 6.27</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	     3.37 vs 3.38</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	     7.28 vs 7.35</p>
<p>    Sales				  123.39 vs 71.18</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		  gain 7.51 vs nil</p>
<p>Dividend is fully franked</p>
<p>Pay date not applicable</p>
<p>Reg date not applicable  </p>
<p>NOTE: Maxilink Ltd is a portfolio investment company. Dividend information refers to income units which are no longer on issue following a buyback. The company's only listed securities are its capital units which trade under the code . The company is not an operating company and sales and profits arise from decisions to sell investments which the company believes has no relevance to an investment company.</p>
<p>Net tangible assets (NTA) as at June 30 were A$1.15 a share.</p>
<p>Maxilink is 39.8 percent owned by directors Brian Sherman and Laurence Freedman.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
